  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1221120,
    "UIName": "SpacerMax",
    "Id": "chassisdef_spacermax_SP-2",
    "Name": "SpacerMax",
    "Details": "The SpacerMax SP-2 mounts a fluid gun in the left torso with four tons of ammunition for oil, coolant, bonding agents, cleaning solutions and water. A spot welder replaces the right hand for construction work, while a small laser in the left arm handles debris clearing and precision cutting or demolition.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Easy to Maintain</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.75</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_jackrabbit"
  },
  "VariantName": "SP-2",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "IndustrialMech",
      "mr-resize-0.79-0.76-0.86"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Industrial Mech",
  "YangsThoughts": "The SpacerMax was built by MaxTech as a worker 'Mech meant for construction tasks in the vacuum of space, and it helped build the Star League's SDS platforms. Despite being marketed solely for non-atmospheric conditions, it was fully capable of working on the ground too, though that narrow marketing angle ended up hurting its overall sales. Its environmental sealing system was notoriously fragile, and any damage to even one part of it compromised the whole setup, keeping pilots reliant on a delicate lifeline while working out among the stars.",
